  "summary": "Initiative on the first line. Three characters, four goblins, one room. Ends when the fight does.",
  "about": "A fight and nothing else, for trying hit points, conditions, dice, the map and the approval queue without playing an evening first.\n\nThe party are already in the room and already seen. There is no lead-up and no aftermath: it starts on initiative and ends when one side is down.\n\nThe Combat panel opens on round one with everyone placed and the order already rolled -- the same order every time, because a one-shot run twice should be the same evening twice.\n\nThree characters and nobody in them: invite players to them from the Players dialog.\n\nThe goblins are shared with the party deliberately, so players can watch their hit points fall and see them on the map.",
